  "study_notes": {
    "design": "Seven particle-social topologies: global, ring, toroidal von Neumann, wheel, connected random ER-like, Watts-Strogatz small-world, and Barabasi-Albert scale-free.",
    "graph_parameters": "Random mean-degree target 4; Watts-Strogatz k=4, beta=0.15; Barabasi-Albert m=2. Graphs are fixed for each run and seeded independently from particle streams.",
    "primary_inference": "The main estimand is the within-function paired effect across seeds; dimensions are nested within function family, not treated as independent benchmark families.",
    "FE_budget": "Each quality run uses N*(iterations+1)=12,864 objective evaluations; each performance run uses 9,664 evaluations.",
    "limitations": "Pilot runs are exploratory. Confirmatory runs require a frozen code revision and a 30-seed design."
  },
